<!-- ── PROBLEM ────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="problem">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head fu">
      <span class="label">The problem</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Developers undersell their own <em>project.</em></h2>
      <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem; max-width: 600px;">Most developers lead with specs: sqm, finishes, views. Buyers decide based on outcomes: returns, lifestyle, status. When that story is missing, the offer becomes a commodity, price becomes the only conversation, and you lose.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prob-grid">
      <div class="prob-card fu d1">
        <div class="prob-num">01</div>
        <h3 class="prob-title">No system, no value, only listings.</h3>
        <p class="prob-desc">Putting a property on a portal is not sales. Without a designed offer, a funnel, and someone actively following up, you are waiting for the right buyer to show up. Most of them never do.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prob-card fu d2">
        <div class="prob-num">02</div>
        <h3 class="prob-title">The offer has no story.</h3>
        <p class="prob-desc">A location and a price is not an offer. Without a clear value narrative: returns, lifestyle, who this is for and why, buyers have nothing to say yes to. The spec sheet does not close deals.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prob-card fu d3">
        <div class="prob-num">03</div>
        <h3 class="prob-title">You have leads. Nobody is closing them.</h3>
        <p class="prob-desc">Marketing agencies stop at the spreadsheet. Traditional agents spread their time across 30 listings. Neither one is accountable for signed contracts. The gap between interested and sold is where money disappears.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
